From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH perf 002] panvk: skip DESC_STATE invalidation on redundant set binds

CmdBindDescriptorSets2KHR() marked DESC_STATE dirty on every bind, even when
the caller re-bound the sets and dynamic offsets that were already bound.
Engines that rebind the same set per draw then rebuilt the shader descriptor
tables on every draw.

Add cmd_desc_state_bind_is_noop(): compares the set pointers and, for sets
with dynamic buffers, the dynamic offsets that cmd_desc_state_bind_sets()
would write. Only when something actually changes does the bind run and the
state get invalidated. Descriptor contents are not part of the compared
state: they live in the set's device memory and panvk only embeds the set
address in the tables, so a content update does not require a rebuild.

push descriptor binds are untouched: their contents are compared nowhere and
always invalidate.

Purpose: cut per-draw descriptor table rebuilds for redundant binds.
Tested GPU: build only, not yet run on device.
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21.
Mesa base range: 26.3.0-devel (pinned 5a07217f).
Dependencies: none.
Validation test: TBD, on-device render smoke test.

Generated-by: LLM

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_cmd_desc_state.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_cmd_desc_state.c
index 6beab5f..da6ec01 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_cmd_desc_state.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_cmd_desc_state.c
@@ -53,6 +53,35 @@ cmd_desc_state_bind_sets(struct panvk_descriptor_state *desc_state,
    assert(dynoffset_idx == info->dynamicOffsetCount);
 }
 
+/* True when the sets being bound are already bound with the same dynamic
+ * offsets. Descriptor set contents are not part of this state, so a repeated
+ * bind cannot disturb the shader tables and does not need a DESC_STATE
+ * invalidation. */
+static bool
+cmd_desc_state_bind_is_noop(const struct panvk_descriptor_state *desc_state,
+                            const VkBindDescriptorSetsInfoKHR *info)
+{
+   unsigned dynoffset_idx = 0;
+
+   for (unsigned i = 0; i < info->descriptorSetCount; ++i) {
+      unsigned set_idx = i + info->firstSet;
+      VK_FROM_HANDLE(panvk_descriptor_set, set, info->pDescriptorSets[i]);
+
+      if (desc_state->sets[set_idx] != set)
+         return false;
+
+      if (set) {
+         for (unsigned b = 0; b < set->layout->dyn_buf_count; b++) {
+            if (desc_state->dyn_buf_offsets[set_idx][b] !=
+                info->pDynamicOffsets[dynoffset_idx++])
+               return false;
+         }
+      }
+   }
+
+   return true;
+}
+
 static struct panvk_descriptor_set *
 cmd_get_push_desc_set(struct vk_command_buffer *vk_cmdbuf,
                       struct panvk_descriptor_state *desc_state,
@@ -351,17 +380,23 @@ panvk_per_arch(CmdBindDescriptorSets2KHR)(
 
